cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this teardown, the PayTear toolkit, the JSON corpus, or the video, please cite the paper entry below."
title: "PayTear: a JVM-free TypeScript pipeline for the static teardown of commercial Android payment clients (ZaloPay 11.17.0)"
abstract: >-
  We present a reproducible, dependency-free static analysis pipeline for split
  Android artifacts and apply it to ZaloPay 11.17.0 (vn.com.vng.zalopay), a
  production Vietnamese wallet. The pipeline re-implements ZIP, Android binary XML,
  resources.arsc, Dalvik EXecutable, ELF and the APK Signature Scheme v2/v3 in
  TypeScript and emits a deterministic JSON corpus. The subject contains 63,827
  class definitions, 287,480 methods, 9.26 million decoded instructions, 27 native
  libraries and 62 SDK fingerprints across 17 vendors. We document ten findings,
  including a 32-bit-only native distribution, globally permitted cleartext
  traffic, exported test/tooling activities, ten non-production endpoints shipped
  in the release DEX, card emulation with requireDeviceUnlock=false, 3.9 MB of
  unreachable React Native code, and an anti-tamper stack whose Java entry points
  are absent from the DEX.
